  "conclusion": "The asynchronous stream works correctly and overlaps CPU work, but it does not reduce frame time. Repeated clipping repair is not the remaining primary explanation: v3 has zero warm repairs and still takes 10.19% more cycles than its same-ELF control. Shared raw ownership plus ordered output backpressure serializes later legacy LOADs behind queued raster work. A larger PSRAM bandwidth claim cannot be inferred from these counters.",
  "next_hypothesis": "Decouple the legacy raw lease from draining all earlier GPU packets. Priority at safe raw-engine boundaries would require immutable/restored contexts and a tested release/materialization path before ingress-full waits. This is a proposed structural change, not implemented or credited as a speedup.",
